  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming the Fashion Sector to Drive Positive Outcomes for Biodiversity, Climate, and Oceans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Develop and implement effective science-based tools to enable companies to drive delivery of the Fashion Pact&#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x2122;s biodiversity, climate, and ocean commitments.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project has an exceptional potential to transform the fashion industry and generate benefits that will have long-term and significant environmental benefit while also providing important positive socioeconomic outcomes.  The sourcing of sustainably produced raw materials by the fashion industry will spur growth and jobs associated with these industries.  Meanwhile, the purchasing of these sustainably produced products will result in improved animal welfare (cashmere) and reduce d deforestation and land conversion.  Finally, the switch to gold sourcing that reduces the use of mercury will improve the environment and especially water quality for local mining communities while reducing their exposure to toxic levels of these minerals. As the Fashion Pact grows, the magnitude of its impact will grow and expand into additional commodities that will result in more accessible, viable, and healthy socioeconomic benefits for people around the world.</narrative>
  </description>
